  "hindi": "वीरों के साथ वह विरोधी के वीरों को जीत ले; गायों के साथ वह धन फैलाए और स्वयं सावधान रहे। उसकी सन्तान और उसका वंशज बढ़ता है, जिस-जिस को ब्रह्मणस्पति अपना साथी बनाता है।",
  "english": "With heroes he shall win the heroes of the hostile one; with cattle he shall spread wealth and take heed by himself. His offspring and his descendant grow, whomever Brahmaṇaspati makes his companion.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "The object of vanavat is read as 'vīrān' with 'vanuṣyataḥ' in apposition; bodhati tmanā is read as 'take heed by himself'. OPEN: vanuṣyataḥ read as gen. sg. per reviewer (added \"and\" removed); other occurrences are acc. pl.",
